=== Notes ===
# {{note label|april}} Until the [[1996–97 United States network television schedule|1996–97 television season]], ratings were calculated over 30 weeks from September to mid-April. Episodes that aired after mid-April were not part of the overall average and ranking.<ref>{{cite news |title=The big three networks took a big ratings hit this season |work=[[The Charleston Gazette]] |author=Storm, Jonathan |page=P6B |date=May 31, 1997}}</ref>
# {{note label|season2note}} Season one had approximately 13.4 million viewing households.<ref name="season1" /> Season two dropped 9%,<ref>{{cite news |title=Network series take beatings in ratings |work=[[Tulsa World]] |page=2C |date=April 23, 1991}}</ref> resulting in an average of approximately 12.2 million viewing households.
# {{note label|season3note}} Season three had an average rating of 13.0 points.<ref name="season3" /> For the [[1991–92 United States network television schedule|1991–92 season]], each point represented 921,000 viewing households,<ref>{{cite news |title=CBS toasts its win of season ratings |work=[[Tampa Bay Times|St. Petersburg Times]] |author=Williams, Scott |page=17 |date=April 17, 1992}}</ref> resulting in a total average of approximately 12.0 million viewing households.
# {{note label|season5}} Season four had approximately 12.1 million viewing households.<ref name="Year-end ratings" /> Season five dropped 13%,<ref>{{cite news |title=''Home Improvement'' improves to no. 1 spot |work=[[South Florida Sun-Sentinel]] |author=Jicha, Tom |page=1E |date=April 20, 1994}}</ref> resulting in an average of approximately 10.5 million viewing households.<section end=head/>
# {{note label|season36}} Season 36 had eighteen episodes broadcast on Fox, and four are Disney+ exclusives that are not a part of the normal season.
# {{note label|season37}} Season 37 had fifteen episodes broadcast on Fox, and will have a further four Disney+ exclusives that are not a part of the normal season
# {{note label|season38to40}} Seasons 38 through 40 will have fifteen episodes each broadcast on Fox, with an additional two Disney+ exclusives per season that are not a part of the normal season.<ref>{{cite web|first=Jamie|last=Lang|date=June 12, 2025|title='The Fans Are More Intense Than Ever': Matt Groening, David Silverman and Matt Selman on 'The Simpsons' Enduring Appeal|url=https://variety.com/2025/tv/global/the-simpsons-matt-groening-david-silverman-matt-selman-1236429217/|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|access-date=July 7, 2025}}</ref> </onlyinclude>

